<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Linux on Open Bouffalo</title><link>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/</link><description>Recent content in Linux on Open Bouffalo</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Buildroot</title><link>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/buildroot/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/buildroot/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Setting up a Buildroot environment for the BL808 SoC is a practical starting point for developing custom Linux firmware and applications. This guide covers the required tools, the repository layout, the default configuration, and the resulting output artifacts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="overview"
 &gt;
 Overview
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/buildroot/#overview" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Overview" aria-label="Anchor to: Overview" href="#overview"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install the required host tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Download Buildroot and the &lt;code&gt;buildroot_bouffalo&lt;/code&gt; overlay.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Export the overlay path so Buildroot can find the board support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Load the default configuration for the Pine64 Ox64 board.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optionally adjust the configuration with &lt;code&gt;make menuconfig&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the images.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect the output artifacts from &lt;code&gt;output/images/&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="requirements"
 &gt;
 Requirements
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/buildroot/#requirements" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Requirements" aria-label="Anchor to: Requirements" href="#requirements"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Install the following tools before building.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Custom Linux Kernel</title><link>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_linux_kernel/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_linux_kernel/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;When developing for the BL808, you may want to customize the Linux kernel or add your own device drivers. This guide walks through the SDK setup, Linux source checkout, configuration, and kernel build process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="get-the-sdk"
 &gt;
 Get the SDK
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_linux_kernel/#get-the-sdk" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Get the SDK" aria-label="Anchor to: Get the SDK" href="#get-the-sdk"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can download the SDK from the &lt;a
 class="gdoc-markdown__link"
 href="https://github.com/openbouffalo/buildroot_bouffalo/releases"
&gt;OpenBouffalo Buildroot releases&lt;/a&gt; page, or build it from source.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Custom Lowload</title><link>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;To use peripherals that are not connected to the core running Linux on D0, interrupt handling currently needs to happen on the M0 core. This guide shows how to set up the environment for building custom lowload binaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="requirements"
 &gt;
 Requirements
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#requirements" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Requirements" aria-label="Anchor to: Requirements" href="#requirements"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Install the following tools before building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h3 id="source-tools"
 &gt;
 Source tools
 &lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#source-tools" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Source tools" aria-label="Anchor to: Source tools" href="#source-tools"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;git&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h3 id="build-tools"
 &gt;
 Build tools
 &lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#build-tools" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Build tools" aria-label="Anchor to: Build tools" href="#build-tools"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;which&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;sed&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;make&lt;/code&gt; version &lt;code&gt;3.81&lt;/code&gt; or newer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;binutils&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;build-essential&lt;/code&gt; on Debian-based systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;diffutils&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;gcc&lt;/code&gt; version &lt;code&gt;4.8&lt;/code&gt; or newer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;g++&lt;/code&gt; version &lt;code&gt;4.8&lt;/code&gt; or newer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;bash&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;patch&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;gzip&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;bzip2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;perl&lt;/code&gt; version &lt;code&gt;5.8.7&lt;/code&gt; or newer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;tar&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;cpio&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;unzip&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;rsync&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;file&lt;/code&gt;, available as &lt;code&gt;/usr/bin/file&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;bc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;findutils&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;wget&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;python3&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h3 id="config-tools"
 &gt;
 Config tools
 &lt;/h3&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#config-tools" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Config tools" aria-label="Anchor to: Config tools" href="#config-tools"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;ncurses5&lt;/code&gt;, sometimes packaged as &lt;code&gt;ncurses&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ncurses-dev&lt;/code&gt;, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="install-dependencies-on-arch-linux"
 &gt;
 Install dependencies on Arch Linux
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#install-dependencies-on-arch-linux" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Install dependencies on Arch Linux" aria-label="Anchor to: Install dependencies on Arch Linux" href="#install-dependencies-on-arch-linux"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;pacman -Syu git which sed make binutils diffutils gcc bash patch gzip bzip2 perl tar cpio unzip rsync file bc findutils wget ncurses python3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="install-dependencies-on-debian"
 &gt;
 Install dependencies on Debian
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#install-dependencies-on-debian" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Install dependencies on Debian" aria-label="Anchor to: Install dependencies on Debian" href="#install-dependencies-on-debian"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;sudo apt update
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;sudo apt install git sed make binutils diffutils gcc g++ bash patch gzip bzip2 perl tar cpio unzip rsync file bc findutils wget libncurses-dev python3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="get-the-tools-and-source"
 &gt;
 Get the tools and source
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#get-the-tools-and-source" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Get the tools and source" aria-label="Anchor to: Get the tools and source" href="#get-the-tools-and-source"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; ~/buildroot_bouffalo/
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;git clone https://github.com/openbouffalo/OBLFR.git
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;git clone https://github.com/bouffalolab/bl_mcu_sdk.git
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;git clone https://gitee.com/bouffalolab/toolchain_gcc_t-head_linux.git
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="set-up-the-toolchain-path"
 &gt;
 Set up the toolchain path
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#set-up-the-toolchain-path" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Set up the toolchain path" aria-label="Anchor to: Set up the toolchain path" href="#set-up-the-toolchain-path"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;PATH&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$PATH&lt;/span&gt;:&lt;span class="k"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;pwd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;/toolchain_gcc_t-head_linux/bin/
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="build"
 &gt;
 Build
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#build" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Build" aria-label="Anchor to: Build" href="#build"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; OBLFR/apps/m0_lowload
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;make
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="flashing"
 &gt;
 Flashing
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/custom_low_load/#flashing" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Flashing" aria-label="Anchor to: Flashing" href="#flashing"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The resulting files:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Flashing</title><link>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/flashing/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/flashing/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;After you have either &lt;a
 class="gdoc-markdown__link"
 href="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/buildroot/"
&gt;built your own Buildroot images&lt;/a&gt; or downloaded the &lt;a
 class="gdoc-markdown__link"
 href="https://github.com/openbouffalo/buildroot_bouffalo/releases"
&gt;prebuilt binaries&lt;/a&gt;, the next step is flashing them to the board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap"&gt;
 &lt;h2 id="prerequisites"
 &gt;
 Prerequisites
 &lt;/h2&gt;
 &lt;a data-clipboard-text="https://openbouffalo.github.io/chips/bl808/linux/flashing/#prerequisites" class="gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center" title="Anchor to: Prerequisites" aria-label="Anchor to: Prerequisites" href="#prerequisites"&gt;
 &lt;svg class="gdoc-icon gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;use xlink:href="#gdoc_link"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before starting, make sure you have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Downloaded the preferred image for your SoC and extracted it, or built it yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Downloaded DevCube from &lt;a
 class="gdoc-markdown__link"
 href="http://dev.bouffalolab.com/download"
&gt;http://dev.bouffalolab.com/download&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connected the BL808 board to your PC over the serial port.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Put the BL808 board into programming mode:
Press the &lt;code&gt;BOOT&lt;/code&gt; button while resetting or applying power, then release &lt;code&gt;BOOT&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flashing does not work with DevCube &lt;code&gt;v1.8.4&lt;/code&gt;, so use &lt;code&gt;v1.8.3&lt;/code&gt; or another known-good version. See &lt;a
 class="gdoc-markdown__link"
 href="https://github.com/openbouffalo/buildroot_bouffalo/issues/60"
&gt;openbouffalo/buildroot_bouffalo#60&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>